A highly-anticipated Alzheimer's drug developed by a millennial biotech CEO has failed in a final-stage trial.
Drug developer Axovant Sciences Ltd, founded by 32-year-old Vivek Ramaswamy, said it would stop testing its lead drug to fight the disease after it failed to meet the main goals they set out.
The major setback has scuppered Axovant's hopes of cashing in on $4 billion in sales per year.
It has also underlined the challenges in developing treatments for the memory-robbing disease.
The company's shares tumbled 74.7 percent to a record low of $6.13 in morning trading on Tuesday.
